        "original_id": "c2b61ec9-dbf8-502c-9f8b-929726b0c30d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Virgilia, Koeleria\n- Places: Southern Africa, Antarctica, oceanic islands\n- Families: Fabaceae, grass family\n\nFacts:\n- Virgilia is a genus of Southern African trees in the family Fabaceae.\n- Virgilia has shiny to hairy pinnate leaves, mauve to pink pea-shaped flowers, and leathery pods.\n- Koeleria is a common and widespread genus of plants in the grass family.\n- Koeleria is found on all continents except Antarctica and on various oceanic islands.",
